-- title:
--   Supersingular completion of full-level moduli ring modulo 1-ζ is reduced
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $5\le q$, a prime $\ell$ with $3\le\ell$ and $\ell\neq q$, and a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$. Let $A_0$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is $(q)$ and whose residue field is finite. Assume: `hℓ`, that for every $A_0$-algebra $T$ a Katz level-$\ell$ datum $D$ (points $P,Q$ satisfying the affine Weierstrass equation, with $(W.\mathrm{pre}\Psi_\ell)(x_P)=(W.\mathrm{pre}\Psi_\ell)(x_Q)=0$ and both independence elements units) remains such after a variable change $C$, applied to $D.\mathrm{variableChange}\,C$; `hM`, the analogous equivariance of `IsGamma0PowAt` (for $p^k\neq 2$: a monic-in-top-degree polynomial $h$ of degree at most $\varphi(p^k)/2$ with $h\cdot\mathrm{pre}\Psi_{p^{k-1}}\mid \mathrm{pre}\Psi_{p^k}$ and $h$ dividing the relevant multiplication numerators; for $p^k=2$ the two-torsion condition) under `kernelVariableChangeDeg`; a family $\mathcal G$ of relative group laws on the projective Weierstrass models of $A_0$-algebras with unit discriminant, which is chord–tangent (compatible with addition and Galois twisting on points over fields) and has its identity section given in the origin chart by $x/y=z/y=0$; a level transport $\mathcal T$ of raw Drinfeld pairs satisfying the section-transport compatibilities with variable-change and coefficient homomorphisms; and `hVC`, `hCO`, the existence of graded ring homomorphisms on the graded model rings realising variable changes and base changes, with the irrelevant ideal of the target contained in the image of the irrelevant ideal of the source. Let $P_0$ be a fine moduli package for the rigid datum `rigidDataPow` combining $\Gamma_0(M')$-type cyclic-kernel polynomials, Katz level-$\ell$ data and Drinfeld $\Gamma(q)$ pairs: a ring $B_0$, an $A_0$-algebra of finite type, with a point $P_0.\mathrm{univ}$ representing the functor $T\mapsto$ (curves with unit discriminant and level data, modulo variable change). Let $x$ be a raw datum over $B_0$ whose class equals $P_0.\mathrm{univ}$, let $\mathfrak m\subset B_0$ be a maximal ideal containing the image of $q$, and let $F_0$ be a formal group over $B_0/\mathfrak m$ whose power series is the fixed formal group law of the reduction of $x.\mathrm{curve}$ modulo $\mathfrak m$ and whose $q$-th iterate `nthSeries q` equals $u\,X^{q^2}$ for some unit $u$. Finally let $\zeta$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity in the $\mathfrak m$-adic completion of $B_0$. Then the quotient of that completion by the ideal generated by $1-\zeta$ is reduced.
--
--   This is the local reducedness statement at a supersingular point of the moduli ring with $\Gamma_0(M')$, level-$\ell$ and Drinfeld $\Gamma(q)$ structure: the completion at such a point is a complete regular local ring of dimension two carrying a Drinfeld basis for its formal group, and cutting it by the uniformiser $1-\zeta$ of $\mathbb Z[\zeta_q]$ leaves a reduced ring. It feeds the companion statement about the residue field base change of this quotient, which is the form used for the geometry of the moduli scheme in characteristic $q$.
